Some of this may be spoilers on gems and such...


>Never seen one pick up a gem by itself, but they love it if you throw gems
>to them. This can increase or decrease luck - If you can, throw identified
>gems at co-aligned unicorns.

Right, I knew about throwing them. That's what I meant when I said I
knew unicorns liked gems. It has been confirmed elsewhere that they
will collect them (I guess "steal" isn't really the right word, since
they weren't on my person) from floors. This actually is a way of
halfway identifying gems -- unicorns only seem to pick up valuable
ones by choice, although they will accept non-valuable ones if thrown.
The catch, of course, is that you have to get the gems back then.

It's kind of a catch-22. Thrown gems are supposedly worth more if they
are identified as valuable. But if you know they're valuable, are you
really going to throw them? I prefer to throw a dozen that I know are
worthless pieces of glass than one I know isn't. And of course,
"knowing" isn't the same as having them identified. You can usually
tell the worthless ones just because they appear so frequently.

